{"schemaVersion":1,"release":"20261114-evidence2","scope":"Three bounded number-state learning panels, structure-source handoff into explicit representation calculations, and an official Cu thermal-file workflow.","counts":{"oscillatorLessons":3,"oscillatorPlacements":3,"cuInputCellAtoms":4,"cuRows":251},"hooks":{"scattering-temperature":["ladder-weights"],"polaron-hamiltonian":["vacuum-motion"],"polaron-truncation":["finite-boundary"]},"verification":["Independent number-state sums and matrices check amplitudes, probabilities, separately weighted tails, microscopic reverse transitions and finite-boundary commutators against the fixed references and the existing Python API.","Course integration preserves disclosures, unfinished responses, notes and original calculator drafts; explicit copying preserves the exact chosen temperature and waits for manual calculation.","Strict source metadata preserves file/text hash identity, tolerances, basis/origin and wavevector transforms and single/double-valued selection through workbench export and explicitly saved research records. Changed requests cannot inherit unrelated source metadata.","Official Cu source bytes, lossless XZ decompression, input-cell normalization and all thermal rows are checked. Import loading, replacement, cancellation and stale completion are exercised through actual form handlers."],"boundaries":["Fixed teaching references do not introduce a general oscillator or scattering solver. Holstein vacuum and numerical truncation panels do not infer a finite-temperature polaron state.","A source checksum identifies the parsed source; it is not an electronic-structure calculation or magnetic-order detector. Imported metadata cannot independently reverify absent original bytes. Numerical representation validity and standard-label coverage remain separate.","Cu thermal_properties data describe one official calculated four-atom input cell at one volume. They do not supply eigenvectors, measured data, full quasi-harmonic volume predictions or a newly performed material calculation.","This release covers three learning hooks and representative source workflows. Broader curriculum depth, diagnosis and authentic workflows for every tool family remain open."],"files":{"GOAL-ROADMAP.md":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":31483,"sha256":"b74244e5134f074ac9ed113e1308004b5e7ed4cfdeda3281d05fee08944d1e7d"},"dist/app.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":97240,"sha256":"448933ce8c77409fc848649b8cb3257dee11694cd3c6116911a3cfa421e8f721"},"dist/bridges-ui.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":17145,"sha256":"fe356c0c36ce7a136726c3cee7d2a53932325e6ce88dab9002010b599ca6e73d"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-LICENSE.txt":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":1470,"sha256":"2ce26839c8b70d28765d73e934cc1a979d896d8d228d30694fdd9a92e94d43a9"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-thermal-index05.yaml":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":41975,"sha256":"1c9e6edeeded194fc7eebe9c4f4bd6e88728b48ea4f530a033240f8394267bf1"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-thermal-index05.yaml.xz":{"normalization":"raw-bytes","bytes":4900,"sha256":"36c87fc5560cc7815cd9d97105830c00cffa4a3a2fb486235d7976bc493ebb1f"},"dist/data/examples/phonopy-cu-thermal-source.json":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":2907,"sha256":"903330e565a126b3e8d30b09099ce1a352fbf0703c9d98e4cf2344e56941763f"},"dist/docs/cu-thermal-example.md":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":4040,"sha256":"69155f09dba2ab02a9a59e71a7f55b2a16ebf5bf177b295c1144eb892027a017"},"dist/index.html":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":7189,"sha256":"d6ee605d0aa60b1f112a7e40b7c7616fb008fa85763fbfce56b0a9620320d41d"},"dist/learning-bridge-host.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":4616,"sha256":"b549c0f3268b4ccf3b2e801bf6a5cb91d2be1a666903fb0e03b70f26467b70e8"},"dist/material-notebook.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":24766,"sha256":"5ef2db44051ff1c65d17c0d14a13b42e114acbaae435202b7d242de678bf178c"},"dist/material-research-ui.js":{"normalization":"utf